      <marc:subfield code="a">A collection of short and medium-length stories by Keigo Higashino, published for the first time to commemorate the author’s 25th anniversary since debut. The eight stories reflect different stages of Higashino’s writing career, each one intricately crafted and uniquely distinctive. A kind-hearted female lawyer takes in a lost, amnesiac girl on a rainy night—only to find a blood-stained dagger hidden in the girl&apos;s handkerchief. A daughter survives a car accident, but upon waking, she seems to be possessed by the spirit of her deceased mother. A couple is lucky enough to adopt a newborn baby, but behind the infant’s angelic face lies a sorrowful plan for revenge...</marc:subfield>
